/**
 * @mainpage Complementary Filter Library
 *
 * @section intro Introduction
 *
 * This library provides a generic implementation of a first-order
 * complementary filter for sensor fusion.
 *
 * A complementary filter combines measurements from different sensors
 * by exploiting their complementary frequency characteristics. A
 * low-frequency measurement from one sensor can be combined with a
 * high-frequency measurement from another sensor to obtain a more
 * stable estimate.
 *
 * The library provides a templated @ref estimators::cf::CF class that
 * supports different numeric types such as @c float and @c double.
 *
 *
 * @section features Features
 *
 * The complementary filter library provides:
 *
 * - First-order complementary filtering.
 * - Fusion of two sensor measurements.
 * - Configurable cutoff frequency.
 * - Configurable sampling time.
 * - Configurable filter time constant.
 * - Configurable complementary filter coefficient.
 * - Runtime parameter modification.
 * - Filter state reset functionality.
 * - Getter functions for filter parameters.
 * - Support for different numeric data types through templates.
 *
 *
 * @section usage Basic Usage
 *
 * A complementary filter can be created and initialized using a cutoff
 * frequency and sampling time:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "cf.h"
 *
 * estimators::cf::CF<double> filter;
 *
 * filter.init(2.5, 0.006);
 *
 * double output = filter.update(x1, x2);
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section parameters Filter Parameters
 *
 * The filter can be configured using the following parameters:
 *
 * - @c fc   : Cutoff frequency of the filter.
 * - @c tau  : Time constant of the filter.
 * - @c dt   : Sampling time or control-loop period.
 * - @c alpha: Complementary filter coefficient.
 *
 * The parameters can be configured during initialization or individually
 * using the corresponding setter functions.
 *
 *
 * @section configuration Parameter Configuration
 *
 * The filter can be initialized using:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * filter.init(fc, dt);
 * @endcode
 *
 * Alternatively, individual parameters can be configured using:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * filter.set_fc(fc);
 * filter.set_tau(tau);
 * filter.set_dt(dt);
 * filter.set_alpha(alpha);
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section update Updating the Filter
 *
 * New sensor measurements are provided to the filter using the
 * @ref estimators::cf::CF::update function:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double output = filter.update(x1, x2);
 * @endcode
 *
 * The two input measurements are combined according to the configured
 * complementary filter parameters, and the filtered output is returned.
 *
 *
 * @section reset Resetting the Filter
 *
 * The internal filter state can be reset using:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * filter.reset();
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section access Accessing Parameters
 *
 * The current filter parameters can be obtained using:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * double fc    = filter.get_fc();
 * double tau   = filter.get_tau();
 * double dt    = filter.get_dt();
 * double alpha = filter.get_alpha();
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section classes Main Class
 *
 * The main class provided by this library is:
 *
 * - @ref estimators::cf::CF - Generic complementary filter for sensor fusion.
 *
 *
 * @section namespace Namespace
 *
 * The complementary filter implementation is contained in:
 *
 * @code
 * estimators::cf
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section example Complete Example
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "cf.h"
 *
 * int main()
 * {
 *     estimators::cf::CF<double> filter;
 *
 *     filter.init(2.5, 0.006);
 *
 *     double x1 = 10.0;
 *     double x2 = 10.5;
 *
 *     double output = filter.update(x1, x2);
 *
 *     return 0;
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 *
 * @section documentation Documentation
 *
 * Detailed documentation for the complementary filter class and its
 * member functions is available through the
 * @ref estimators::cf::CF class reference.
 *
 *
 * @copyright
 * Copyright (c) 2026 Abhinay Kumar
 *
 * @author Abhinay Kumar
 * @version 1.0
 * @date 2026-08-11
 */